{"text": "First break. In 1929, a man at a great telescope in California used SEF-ee-id distances to show the galaxies flee from us. The farther, the faster. The universe expands. Run that film backwards, and you get an age. His rate gave: not quite two billion years. Awkward, even then. The geologists put the Earth itself at around two billion. By the mid-fifties it turned absurd. The Earth's true age came in at four and a half billion. Run those numbers, and you are standing on a planet older than the universe around it. Part of the fault lay on LEV-it's rung. There are two families of pulsing stars, with two different rulers. Mixing them had shrunk the cosmos. In 1952, in a hall in Rome, a man stood up and pulled the families apart. At a stroke, the universe doubled. Still too small. In 1958, another astronomer found: the California man had also mistaken glowing gas clouds for bright stars. The rate fell again, and the universe came out comfortably older than the Earth. Total correction, first to last: about a factor of seven.", "alignment": {"characters": ["F", "i", "r", "s", "t", " ", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", ".", " ", "I", "n", " ", "1", "9", "2", "9", ",", " ", "a", " ", "m", "a", "n", " ", "a", "t", " ", "a", " ", "g", "r", "e", "a", "t", " ", "t", "e", "l", "e", "s", "c", "o", "p", "e", " ", "i", "n", " ", "C", "a", "l", "i", "f", "o", "r", "n", "i", "a", " ", "u", "s", "e", "d", " ", "S", "E", "F", "-", "e", "e", "-", "i", "d", " ", "d", "i", "s", "t", "a", "n", "c", "e", "s", " ", "t", "o", " ", "s", "h", "o", "w", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "g", "a", "l", "a", "x", "i", "e", "s", " ", "f", "l", "e", "e", " ", "f", "r", "o", "m", " ", "u", "s", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", " ", "f", "a", "r", "t", "h", "e", "r", ",", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "f", "a", "s", "t", "e", "r", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", " ", "u", "n", "i", "v", "e", "r", "s", "e", " ", "e", "x", "p", "a", "n", "d", "s", ".", " ", "R", "u", "n", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "f", "i", "l", "m", " ", "b"